{"kind":"assert","text":"AR-6 finding (b3b90323), read-only: DO analytics per object and namespace, 17:09-17:12Z and 17:33-17:43Z, plus the simulator source.\n\nEach hourly pair is the Grow demo's scripted fault cycle, not background work. dap-grow-simulator ticks each minute (cron \"* * * * *\"). Its schedule (examples/grow/simulator.ts, simulator-release.test.ts:34) starts the vent fault at minute 10, frees the vent at minute 35 and resets the fan trip at minute 40. Each event makes incident and agent work in the room for about two minutes.\n\nPer object, requests a minute, at rest and then in the pair:\n- ScopeIndex 71671c0f (namespace df59f306): 24, then 33/30 at :35 and 28/27 at :40; at :10, 26 then 38/33.\n- Room A e90a0152 (DeployedScope): 13, then 21/19 at :35 and 16/16 at :40; at :10, 13 then 26/22.\n- Membership e3b2c953: 4, then 5 in the first minute of each pair.\n- Site 236dc9fd and Directory 661c0b32: 4 each, flat. AR-5 holds.\n\nSo the pairs are about 30 to 40 requests an hour, on the scenario the demo shows.\n\nThe bigger cost is the floor. Of 49 a minute, ScopeIndex takes 24 and Room A 13 for one observation a minute. That is about 1,440 ScopeIndex requests an hour, about two per room request. I have not yet traced which calls reach ScopeIndex per tick.\n\nOptions:\n(a) Leave the pairs; they are the demo's designed traffic. Close AR-6 as explained.\n(b) Retarget AR-6 at the ScopeIndex floor: trace the index reads per simulator tick and propose a change that cuts them. That is code in apps/room, and I can start the read now.\n(c) Lengthen the simulator period. That is a demo product change for Hugh, and it changes the fault story.\nI recommend (a) with (b). Which do you want?","body":{"to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}